Phase 4.4 — packaging split: implementation+verification vs operator-gated signing
========================================================================
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 4 item 4, SPLIT per operator directive
(2026-09-10): (1) packaging implementation and verification with
unsigned/development artifacts — complete now; (2) production
signing/notarization = BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_CREDENTIAL / RELEASE_GATE — an
OPERATOR step on an operator-controlled machine. No Apple Developer
private credentials, notarization secrets, or Windows signing private
keys may ever enter the agent runtime, this repository, or CI.
Revision: the Phase 4.4 commit on main (after 7078d77)
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT WAS BUILT
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- tools/release/package.sh: deterministic bundle assembly —
  build (debug or release) → dist/modbit-<version>-<target>/ layout
  (bin/{modbit,modbit-core,modbit-execd}) → SBOM (cargo-cyclonedx when
  present, else a deterministic Cargo.lock-derived fallback JSON) →
  provenance.json (git rev, profile, target, rustc commit, built_at,
  signed:false, signing_state BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_CREDENTIAL/RELEASE_GATE)
  → SHA256SUMS over every file (sorted).
- tools/release/verify-bundle.sh: hash verification of every file →
  provenance completeness → binary smoke (with stray-process guards) →
  signature STATE check. The state check requires a REAL Developer ID
  authority (macOS) / Authenticode (Windows): an AD-HOC local signature
  (present on all dev builds) is reported as "AD-HOC signed
  (development build)" and does NOT count as production signing.
- tools/release/operator-signing.md: the operator contract — the exact
  credential-bearing commands (codesign --options runtime --timestamp
  --sign "Developer ID Application: …", notarytool submit + stapler;
  Windows signtool /fd SHA256 with timestamping) to run on an operator
  machine, plus the release flow:
  build → test → package → SBOM/hash/provenance → operator signing →
  notarization/signature verification → release receipt.
- tools/release/release-receipt.sh: the flow's final artifact — a JSON
  receipt with bundle hash, provenance, signature_verified (Developer
  ID/Authenticode only) and release_gate (PRODUCTION_OK vs
  BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_CREDENTIAL).

VERIFICATION (live, this machine)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- package.sh --dev → dist/modbit-0.1.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/ with
  bin/{modbit,modbit-core,modbit-execd}, SBOM fallback JSON (valid),
  provenance.json, SHA256SUMS.
- verify-bundle.sh → hashes OK, provenance complete, binaries execute,
  signature state "AD-HOC signed (development build)" (correct: no
  Developer ID here).
- release-receipt.sh → signature_verified:false,
  release_gate:BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_CREDENTIAL (correct for a dev bundle).
- Script fixes recorded: repo-root cd via git rev-parse; binary smoke
  with stray-process guards; the authority-based signature check (an
  ad-hoc signature verifies trivially and must not count as production
  signing).

SECURITY BOUNDARIES (per operator directive)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- No Apple/Windows private credentials were requested, stored, exposed,
  imported, or handled in the agent runtime, repository, or CI.
- Signing blocks ONLY the production release gate — implementation and
  verification of the packaging flow are complete and reproducible
  without credentials.

REMAINING (gated)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The operator performs the credential-bearing signing + notarization on
an operator machine, runs verify-bundle.sh (must report SIGNED), and
generates the release receipt with release_gate=PRODUCTION_OK.
